.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
outputs/
.cache/
.claude/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
# Throwaway interpreters. A worktree that needs a second set of pins
# (a lockfile bump, a sibling lane's branch) builds `.venv-<something>`
# beside the real one; none of them belongs in a commit.
.venv-*/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Hypothesis's working directory (ADR 0069): the `constants/` and
# `unicode_data/` caches every profile writes, and — under `explore`
# only — the example database. `git status` is already clean without
# this line, because Hypothesis creates the directory containing a
# `.gitignore` of `*`. The line is here because that generated file
# says of itself that Hypothesis "will not re-create this .gitignore
# unless .hypothesis is deleted". Measured: delete that one file and
# the directory shows up as `?? .hypothesis/` and stays there, because
# a later property run repopulates the caches without restoring the
# ignore. An ignore rule the repository owns does not depend on a
# dependency's housekeeping. The example database is never restored in
# CI — `tests/property/conftest.py` says why.
.hypothesis/

# Pilot credentials (WO-W17). The bcrypt file the edge reads and the
# cleartext keystore FastAPI hot-reloads. Both are generated per
# deployment by docs/runbooks/pilot.md and neither may ever be committed;
# the patterns are broad so a dated suffix cannot slip past.
deploy/pilot/pilot-users*.caddy
deploy/pilot/pilot-keys*.json

# Web (Next.js) — mirrored in web/.gitignore for editors that
# don't traverse subdir ignores.
web/node_modules/
web/.next/
web/out/
web/coverage/
web/next-env.d.ts

# Private project notes — the top-level agent/project context file is
# local-only by owner decision; public entry points are README.md and
# docs/README.md. All casings ignored so a rename cannot re-track it.
CLAUDE.md
claude.md
CLAUDE-Agent-Proj-1.md
